Here's how the C# function including assert can be written:

```cs
using System.IO;
using System.Diagnostics;

void LoadTemplates(string fileName)
{
    bool templatesFileExist = File.Exists(fileName);
    Debug.Assert(templatesFileExist, "The template file does not exist");
    // If the template file doesn't exist, this line of code will generate an AssertionFailedException
}
```

Note that the Assertions will only work if you have enabled the "Debug" mode in your Visual Studio. Also, assertions are not recommended for production code as they are removed in Release mode to improve performance. They are most commonly used for testing purposes to identify mistakes in the code.--------------------